### HIGH: coderabbit (coderabbitai[bot])
**File**: `tests/e2e/shared-conversations.spec.js:474`
_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**`page.unroute()` with regex won't remove the function-based route.**

The route registered by `interceptSharedSessionsList()` uses a function matcher (line 117), but `page.unroute()` here uses a regex. Playwright requires the exact same matcher reference to remove a route—a regex won't match a function.

The route won't be removed, so both handlers remain active. Playwright invokes the most recently added route first, which happens to make this test pass, but the behavior is fragile and the intent (replace the route) isn't achieved.



<details>
<summary>Suggested fix: use `page.unrouteAll()` or re-register with same URL filter</summary>

Option 1 – Remove all routes for this URL pattern explicitly:

```diff
-		// Remove the beforeEach route so our counting handler takes precedence.
-		await page.unroute( /gratis-ai-agent\/v1\/sessions\/shared/ );
+		// Remove all routes so our counting handler takes precedence.
+		// page.unroute() requires the same matcher reference; unrouteAll removes all.
+		await page.unrouteAll( { behavior: 'wait' } );
```

Option 2 – Keep the function matcher consistent (avoids removing unrelated routes):

```diff
-		await page.unroute( /gratis-ai-agent\/v1\/sessions\/shared/ );
+		// The beforeEach route uses a function matcher; Playwright requires the
+		// same reference to unroute. Instead, we rely on route precedence: the
+		// later-added route below will be invoked first.
```

</details>

